    "sections": [
      {
        "label": "1st quarter",
        "score": "BOS 24, ORL 23",
        "text": "Boston went 1-of-10 from three but forced eight turnovers. Hugo González, in his first start of the season, scored all 7 of his points in the quarter. Tatum bumped heads with Jamal Cain and went to the locker room bleeding, then returned without needing stitches."
      },
      {
        "label": "2nd quarter",
        "score": "BOS 55, ORL 50",
        "text": "Payton Pritchard picked up three fouls in 10:40 and sat the rest of the half. Boston stayed ahead on the glass, with eight offensive rebounds and 13 second-chance points by halftime; Tatum had 17 and Luka Garza 9 off the bench."
      },
      {
        "label": "3rd quarter",
        "score": "BOS 77, ORL 74",
        "text": "Boston opened the half on a 14–4 run, capped by a Derrick White three, to lead 69–54. Tristan da Silva hit three threes in 2:28 and Anthony Black added another to tie it 72–72. Boston's only field goal over the last 7:03 was a Sam Hauser three, and Tatum scored the quarter's final 5 points at the line."
      },
      {
        "label": "4th quarter",
        "score": "Final: BOS 108, ORL 97",
        "text": "Black tied it at 79 early in the quarter, and Orlando later got within 97–93. Tatum answered with two mid-range jumpers, and George's three with 1:32 left made it 104–93. George scored 10 in the quarter, and Neemias Queta had two blocks in the final minutes."
      }
